Journey: A claim filed on the portal reaches the API, the database, Kafka and the customer's inbox
Id: claim-submit-ui-to-api-db
Tags: @portal @claims @integration @regression @kafka @email
Role: policyholder
Risk: 5
Requirements: FNOL-1, FNOL-2, FNOL-5, NOTIF-1, EVT-1
Variables: amount=2450.75, policy=POL-H-100231

Set variable incidentDate to format(addDays(today(), -6), "YYYY-MM-DD")
Set variable story to "Burst pipe under the kitchen sink, run " + unique("K")
Start listening on Kafka topic "larkspur.claims.events" on events as claimEvents

Log in
Click the "Make a claim" link
  Expect the page contains "Make a claim"
Select "POL-H-100231 - Home" from the Policy dropdown
Select "Water damage" from the "Claim type" dropdown
Fill the "Incident date" field with ${incidentDate}
  Expect the page contains "Reporting deadline"
Fill the "Amount claimed (GBP)" field with ${amount}
Fill the "What happened?" field with "${story}"
Upload "fixtures/kitchen-water-damage.png" and "fixtures/plumber-invoice.txt" to the "Supporting documents" field
  Expect the page contains "plumber-invoice.txt"

# The coverage guide opens in a popup window
Click the "Coverage guide" link and switch to the popup
  Expect the page contains "Coverage guide: Home insurance"
Expect the page contains "Claims must be reported within 30 days"
Close the popup
Switch back to the main tab

# The declaration lives in an iframe and tells the form through postMessage
In the "Declaration" frame
  Check the "I agree to the declaration" checkbox
  Click the "Confirm declaration" button
    Expect the page contains "Declaration confirmed."
End

Click the "Submit claim" button
  Expect the URL matches "/app/claims/CLM-\d+"
  Expect the page contains "submitted"
Capture the text of css=h1 matching "CLM-\d+" as claimId
Expect the "Status" text is visible

# The API (partner view) sees the same claim, with the documents' hashes
Call API "GET ${API_URL}/v1/claims/${claimId}" as broker and store as apiClaim
Expect the apiClaim response status is 200
Expect response apiClaim matches schema "schemas/claim.schema.json"
Expect response apiClaim "$.status" equals "SUBMITTED"
Expect response apiClaim "$.channel" equals "PORTAL"
Expect response apiClaim "$.amountClaimed" equals "${amount}"
Expect response apiClaim "$.documents[0].filename" equals "kitchen-water-damage.png"
Expect response apiClaim "$.documents[1].filename" equals "plumber-invoice.txt"

# The database row and its documents
Get the first row of query "SELECT * FROM claims WHERE id = '${claimId}'" on claims as dbClaim
Expect ${dbClaim.status} equals "SUBMITTED"
Expect ${dbClaim.amount_claimed} == ${amount}
Expect ${dbClaim.description} equals "${story}"
Expect ${dbClaim.late_notification} == 0
Expect query "CLAIM_DOCUMENTS" on claims with claim_id="${claimId}" returns 2 rows

# The event, correlated by claim id, and its contract
Wait for a message in claimEvents where "$.claimId" = "${claimId}" and header "event-type" = "claim.submitted" within 20 s matching schema "schemas/claim-event.schema.json" as submitted
Expect response submitted "$.documents" equals "2"
Expect ${submitted_meta.key} equals "${claimId}"
Stop listening to claimEvents

# The acknowledgement e-mail
Wait for an email to "amelia.hart@mail.larkspur.test" with subject "Claim ${claimId} received" within 20 seconds as ack
Expect ${ack.text} contains "${claimId}"
Expect ${ack.text} contains "2450.75 GBP"
